guides=[
 ('wallpaper-tools.html','What should you check before a peel-and-stick project?','Walls & finishes','Start with your surface, then choose your tools.',[
 ('Start with the wall, not the cart','What surface will the covering go on? Find the covering manufacturer’s installation instructions and check whether your wall finish is supported. If that information is missing, pause rather than assume it will work.'),
 ('Make a project checklist','Write down the wall area, corners, outlets and edges you need to work around. Ask which smoothing and trimming tools the covering manufacturer specifies. Do not infer tool compatibility from a product name alone.'),
 ('Compare the kit with the job','The submitted short link resolved to an Art3d smoothing tool kit listing. This is an observed destination, not confirmation that it is the intended item. Open the listing and check the included pieces against your project instructions.'),
 ('Before you buy','Confirm the exact model, included tools, current seller and return terms on the listing. No installation or safety claim has been independently tested here.')]),
 ('paper-towel-mounting.html','Adhesive or screw-mounted: what should you compare?','Kitchen organization','A buying checklist for your paper towel holder.',[
 ('Choose a location first','Where would the roll be easiest to reach? Measure the proposed space with a roll in place, allowing room to replace it. Look for cabinet doors, handles and other objects that could get in the way.'),
 ('Ask about the surface','Which surfaces does the manufacturer explicitly support for the adhesive? What preparation and curing instructions apply? If you rent, check the lease before attaching anything. Do not treat adhesive mounting as a guarantee of damage-free removal.'),
 ('Check the supplied hardware','Does the exact variant include adhesive, screws or both? If drilling, follow the installation instructions and check the mounting surface before proceeding. This guide does not establish that either method is suitable for your home.'),
 ('Read the actual listing','The observed destination is an under-cabinet paper towel holder. Its submitted product intent remains unconfirmed. Check the current variant and instructions directly before purchase.')]),
 ('pan-rack-fit.html','Will a pan organizer actually fit your cabinet?','Kitchen organization','Measure the space you have, not the space you hope for.',[
 ('Measure the opening and the interior','Record the usable cabinet width, depth and height as well as the door opening. Where are the hinges, shelves and plumbing? A useful comparison starts with your actual cabinet, not a photograph.'),
 ('Count handles and lids too','List the cookware you want to store. Measure each piece including handles and lids. Ask the manufacturer about allowed cookware size and load limits; do not infer them from an illustration.'),
 ('Compare arrangements','Would a horizontal or vertical arrangement let you take out the pan you use most? Sketch the arrangement and allow space to lift items out. Confirm the exact rack variant supports the arrangement in its instructions.'),
 ('Check before checkout','The submitted link resolved to an ORDORA cookware organizer listing. We have not tested it or confirmed the submitted product intent. Verify the exact model, dimensions and instructions on the official listing.')]),
 ('air-fryer-checklist.html','Basket or oven-style air fryer: what should you compare?','Kitchen planning','A question-led worksheet, not a product recommendation.',[
 ('Define your meals','Which foods and portion sizes do you actually plan to cook? Write down a typical meal before comparing advertised capacity. Ask for the usable cooking-area dimensions rather than assuming a stated volume answers every question.'),
 ('Map the counter space','How much space do the manufacturer’s instructions require around the appliance? Measure the intended location, including door or basket movement. Check the exact model’s manual; no clearance figures are supplied here.'),
 ('Plan for cleanup','Which parts are removable? Which cleaning methods does the manual allow? Consider where you would wash and dry them. Do not assume a part is dishwasher-safe because another model’s is.'),
 ('Keep the comparison honest','Which functions will you actually use? Compare exact-model manuals, warranty terms and current listings. No submitted link was observed to resolve to an air fryer, and we recommend no air fryer product in this guide.')])]
def guidecards(items=guides[:3]):return '<div class="grid">'+''.join(f'<article class="guide-card"><span class="number">0{i+1}</span><div class="eyebrow">{g[2]}</div><h3><a href="{g[0]}">{g[1]} ↗</a></h3><p>{g[3]}</p><span class="note">DIY HOME Editorial · Buying checklist</span></article>' for i,g in enumerate(items))+'</div>'
page('index.html','Small upgrades. A home that works better.',f'''<section class="hero"><div class="hero-copy"><div class="eyebrow">THE CONSIDERED HOME · NOVEMBER EDIT</div><h1>Small upgrades.<br>A little more<br>everyday ease.</h1><p>Practical finds and thoughtful buying guides for the spaces you use most. Less guesswork. More home.</p><a class="button" href="#the-edit">Explore the edit <span class="arrow">↗</span></a></div><div class="hero-art"><img src="assets/room.svg" alt="Original illustration of a calm sage-green kitchen with an organized countertop"><span class="art-label">THE EVERYDAY KITCHEN · EDITORIAL ILLUSTRATION</span></div></section><div class="trust"><span>↗ &nbsp; Direct links to Amazon listings</span><span>◇ &nbsp; No invented ratings or rankings</span><span>☰ &nbsp; Practical, question-led guides</span></div><section class="section" id="the-edit"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">A PLACE TO START</div><h2>The everyday upgrade edit</h2></div><a href="products.html">Browse the full edit ↗</a></div><div class="filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter products"><button class="chip selected" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All upgrades</button><button class="chip" data-filter="kitchen" aria-pressed="false">Kitchen organization</button><button class="chip" data-filter="walls" aria-pressed="false">Walls & finishes</button></div><p id="filter-status" class="note" role="status">3 products shown</p>{cards()}<p class="note">From the submitted links. Listing destinations observed; intended products and affiliate tracking not yet confirmed. <a href="register.html">See the source notes</a>.</p></section><aside class="band"><div><div class="eyebrow">BEFORE YOU ADD TO CART</div><h2>Measure twice. Buy thoughtfully.</h2><p>A good upgrade starts with the right questions. Our guides help you check the fit, the installation and the everyday trade-offs.</p></div><a class="textlink" href="guides.html">Find your buying guide ↗</a></aside><section class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">THE HOME NOTEBOOK</div><h2>A better question. A better buy.</h2></div><a href="guides.html">All guides ↗</a></div>{guidecards()}</section><aside class="newsletter"><div><div class="eyebrow">KEEP A LITTLE INSPIRATION HANDY</div><h2>Your next small upgrade, in your feed.</h2><p>Follow new guides with RSS. No email address, no inbox clutter.</p></div><a class="button" href="feed.xml">Follow the home notebook ↗</a></aside>''','Thoughtful home upgrades, kitchen organization finds and practical buying guides. Clear sources, no invented product rankings.')
