page('about.html','About & editorial policy',head('OUR POINT OF VIEW','Useful before persuasive.','DIY HOME is an independent home-upgrade publication. The goal is a better purchase decision—not a longer shopping list.')+f'''<div class="prose"><h2>Who writes this site?</h2><p>DIY HOME Editorial is an organizational byline for AI-assisted editorial checklists prepared for this repository. No named expert, credentials, hands-on testing or personal experience is claimed. Product names are abbreviated observed listing titles, not independently tested descriptions.</p><h2>How we choose what to cover</h2><p>This initial edit follows the links supplied for this project. It is not a ranking based on popularity, conversion data or commission. Our guides ask about fit, installation and practical trade-offs. Appliance coverage is an editorial hypothesis, not a claim about the submitted products.</p><h2 id="disclosure">How our links work</h2><p><strong>{D}</strong> Some links may earn a commission when properly configured and eligible. Current product links are direct observed listings, not validated commission-bearing Special Links. They are marked sponsored as a precaution. Account enrollment and tracking ID ownership are not confirmed.</p><h2>Corrections and evidence</h2><p>Check the <a href="register.html">source register</a> and <a href="flagged.html">open review log</a>. Repository issues can be used to request corrections; do not post private account data. {link('https://github.com/kanlerxz87-cyber/DIYHOME1/issues','Repository issues')}</p><p>{link(A,'Amazon Operating Agreement')} · {link(FTC,'FTC guidance')}</p></div>''')
page('privacy.html','Privacy',head('PRIVACY','Less data. Clearer boundaries.','Last updated November 20, 2026.')+'''<div class="prose"><h2>Current static site</h2><p>No analytics endpoint is configured, so the site’s analytics script sends no events. We set no tracking cookies and do not use browser storage. GitHub Pages and its infrastructure may process request data under GitHub’s own policies. External Amazon links open Amazon, which has its own data practices.</p><h2>Optional self-hosted measurement</h2><p>If deployed, the supplied collector accepts five allowlisted events and aggregates them by UTC day, page and product. No visitor ID or session fingerprint is created. There is no email capture. Browser privacy signals disable collection. Invalid payloads are rejected and application request logging is disabled. Hosting or reverse-proxy logs must be separately disabled or minimized before enabling it.</p><h2>Retention and limits</h2><p>The collector deletes aggregate rows older than 90 days on each accepted request. It cannot measure unique visitors, Amazon sessions or individual purchases. Collector deployment requires a same-origin reverse proxy, request-size and rate limits and a privacy review. No service is claimed live.</p><p><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub privacy statement ↗</a> · <a href="analytics.html">Measurement details</a></p></div>''')
